baton_block='<section class="baton-banner" aria-labelledby="baton-title"><span aria-hidden="true">&#129693;</span><div><p class="eyebrow">THE PLUMBING / NEW &middot; CATALOG 38</p><h3 id="baton-title">Play together, not at the same time.</h3><p>The Baton Box is not a workshop &mdash; it is the collection&rsquo;s relay server. It knows no games; it just carries the baton, so one player can set up a position and the next player inherits it, and any pass-and-play game can ride it. (It also serves the game folders with the isolation headers some exhibits need &mdash; it is how the DOS Console runs.) The Relay is its first passenger and the worked example: <em>you don&rsquo;t have to finish it. You have to set up the next person.</em></p><div class="actions"><a class="open light-open" href="projects/baton-box/index.html">Open the Baton Box</a><a href="projects/baton-box/games/the-relay/the-relay.html">Play The Relay &rarr;</a></div></div></section>'
chooser_block='<section class="chooser" aria-labelledby="chooser-title"><p class="eyebrow">LEARNING PATHS / FOUR WAYS IN</p><h2 id="chooser-title">Where are you starting?</h2><div class="paths"><a class="path" href="learning-paths.html#beginner-title"><strong>Just starting</strong><span>The Beginner path on the Learning Paths page.</span></a><a class="path" href="learning-paths.html#intermediate-title"><strong>Comfortable</strong><span>The Intermediate path on the Learning Paths page.</span></a><a class="path" href="learning-paths.html#advanced-title"><strong>The deep end</strong><span>The Advanced path on the Learning Paths page.</span></a><a class="path" href="learning-paths.html#machines-title"><strong>The Machine Path</strong><span>Eleven real consoles, in the order they teach.</span></a><button type="button" class="path surprise" id="surprise"><strong>Surprise me</strong><span>Pick a workshop for me &mdash; any card below.</span></button></div></section>'
taste_block='<section class="taste" aria-labelledby="taste-title"><div class="wn-head"><p class="eyebrow">THE 60-SECOND BENCH / TRY IT HERE</p><a class="text-link" href="projects/packet-playground/index.html">Its home: Packet Playground &rarr;</a></div><h2 id="taste-title">Split a network</h2><p class="taste-lead">You own one block: <strong>192.168.1.0/24</strong> &mdash; 256 addresses. Slide the prefix and watch the trade: every step halves the size and doubles the count. Nothing is free; that is the whole lesson.</p><label class="taste-slider" for="prefix">Prefix <output id="prefixOut">/24</output></label><input id="prefix" type="range" min="24" max="30" step="1" value="24" style="width:100%"><div class="taste-grid"><div><span id="tSubnets">1</span><small>subnet carved out</small></div><div><span id="tSize">256</span><small>addresses in each</small></div><div><span id="tHosts">254</span><small>usable hosts in each</small></div></div><p class="fine" id="tasteNote">At /24 the block is whole: one network, every address in it.</p></section>'
